# keel-overlay-crowdsec: CrowdSec is disabled in a simple installation of
# Keel Core (handbook decisions 0029 and 0041). Debian's presets enable
# every unit they do not name, and systemd applies them on a first boot,
# when /etc/machine-id is missing or says "uninitialized", and on
# `systemctl preset-all`: without these lines either would enable both
# units. keel spec apply enables them where the instance spec says so. See
# packages/README.md in Keel-Linux/common.
disable crowdsec.service
disable crowdsec-firewall-bouncer.service
